  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Load the NASA Exoplanet Archive pscomppars composite table, filter it by discovery method, stellar-age group, radius, period, distance and quality cuts, then compare stellar age and orbital period against planet radius using rank correlations, a host-star bootstrap of the young-to-old radius ratio, and a period-detrended radius-valley histogram. Data used in the run: synthetic. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
